\title{Leave-Out Variance Component Estimation for Two-Way Fixed Effects Models}
\description{
\code{LeaveOutKSS} packages an 'R' translation of the original 'MATLAB' package
of Kline, Saggio, and Solvsten (2020) for leave-out bias correction and
variance decomposition in two-way fixed effects models of the Abowd,
Kramarz, and Margolis (1999; AKM) type.
}
\details{
The package mirrors the logic of the original script-based implementation in
this repository while exposing object-returning, side-effect-free-by-default
workflows. Core estimation functions return structured results and write
files only when users explicitly provide output paths. The main user-facing
workflows are:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=leave_out_KSS]{leave_out_KSS()}} for leave-out bias-corrected decomposition in two-way
fixed effects models.
\item \code{\link[=leave_out_KSS_fe]{leave_out_KSS_fe()}} for the same decomposition when some controls are
supplied as categorical variables to be expanded internally.
\item \code{\link[=rsquared_comp]{rsquared_comp()}} for comparing the fit of a two-way fixed effects model
with a saturated worker-firm specification.
\item \code{\link[=fast_fe_est]{fast_fe_est()}} for recovering fitted values and adjusted outcomes from
one-way or two-way fixed effects models.
}

The implementation follows the structure of the original 'MATLAB' package
and the accompanying vignette material:
\enumerate{
\item Construct the largest connected set of firms.
\item Prune the sample to a leave-one-worker-out connected set.
\item Partial out controls when requested.
\item Compute statistical leverages exactly or by Johnson-Lindenstrauss
approximation (JLA).
\item Form plug-in and leave-out bias-corrected variance component estimates.
}

A small matched worker-firm panel used by the examples is bundled at
\code{system.file("extdata", "test.csv", package = "LeaveOutKSS")}.
}
